# Per-Dockerfile override of the root `.dockerignore`, for `docker/Dockerfile` ONLY — Docker/
# Buildah both look for `<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile before falling
# back to the root file, and use it INSTEAD, not merged with it. This file therefore repeats the
# root list in full; the one deliberate difference is `.git` staying IN.
#
# Why: `npm run complete` — which `docker-compose.test.yml`'s `gate` service and the
# `container-gate` CI job both run inside this image — includes `lint`, and the
# `local/comment-links` ESLint rule shells out to `git ls-files` to check that a
# comment's file reference still exists. No `.git` directory means that rule hard-crashes rather
# than reporting a finding, not a lint failure that could be waived. `docker/Dockerfile.production`
# has the same gap and sidesteps it by never running `lint` at all — see the comment on its build
# stage — which is not an option here because running `npm run complete` unmodified is the point.
#
# GENERATED from the root .dockerignore by scripts/docker/generate-dockerfile-dockerignore.ts —
# `npm run regenerate` rebuilds it. Do not hand-edit.

# Dependencies (installed inside the container)
node_modules

# Secrets
.env

# Per-client deployment config, one directory each. Mounted at runtime, never baked into the image.
clients

# IDE
.idea

# App build output
dist

# VitePress build output and dep cache (both rebuilt inside the docs container)
docs/.vitepress/dist
docs/.vitepress/cache

# Test and analysis output — jest coverage, test/mutation reports, Stryker's own sandbox, per-run
# Mongo data. None of it is read at runtime, and `tmp/reports/` alone is ~20 MB of mutation HTML —
# every megabyte here is copied into the build context on every single build.
tmp

# Generated API-client collections for Bruno, Insomnia, Mockoon and Postman: ~900 KB of developer
# tooling rebuilt by `npm run contracts:bundle -- bruno insomnia mockoon postman`. Only
# `tests/cross-cutting/contract-bundles.test.ts` reads them, and the image build runs no tests —
# `npm run build` is type-check plus lint.
contract.bruno.yml
contract.insomnia.json
contract.mockoon.json
contract.postman.json

# Generated from openapi.yaml fragments by `postinstall` — see .gitignore. A stale host copy would
# be overwritten anyway (`gen:api` starts with `rm -rf ./api`), but there is no reason to upload it
# to the build daemon first.
/openapi.yaml
/api/

# Logs
*.log
